From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Darrel=20Gri=C3=ABt?= <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 23:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] v10: Drop the redundant pre-set vsync wait on minnow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

swap() waits for the vsync callback before calling hwc_device->set().

On minnow's DSI command-mode panel that wait is redundant. The panel
latches from its own GRAM on its TE boundary, and set() already blocks
until the commit completes. The extra wait added ~7 ms per frame to the
render thread, pushing wait+set past one vsync period. Frames then
alternated between 22 and 44 ms (~34 fps).

Let set()'s own TE sync pace the loop. Instrumented swap() phase
averages during a continuous animation:
 before: wall=29.1 wait=7.4 set=16.7 fence=0.0
 after:  wall=22.6 wait=0.0 set=17.4 fence=0.0

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [minnow command-mode panel specific]
Signed-off-by: Darrel Griët <dgriet@gmail.com>
---
 hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp
@@ -239,11 +239,9 @@
 {
     HWC_PLUGIN_ASSERT_ZERO(!(hwc_list->retireFenceFd == -1));
 
-    // Wait for vsync before posting new frame
-    // or force swap if exceeding the vsync timeframe
-    vsync_mutex.lock();
-    vsync_cond.wait(&vsync_mutex, 1000/vsyncFPS);
-    vsync_mutex.unlock();
+    // No vsync wait here: the command-mode panel latches on its own TE
+    // boundary and hwc_device->set() below blocks until the commit lands,
+    // so waiting as well only added ~7 ms of latency per frame.
 
     hwc_list->dpy = EGL_NO_DISPLAY;
     hwc_list->sur = EGL_NO_SURFACE;
